.TH ITCMDR\-ADMINSVR 1 "" "itcmdr" "itcmdr manual"
.SH NAME
itcmdr\-adminsvr \- offsite admin server (admin API, SiteLink, Let's Encrypt)
.SH ITCMDR\-ADMINSVR
.nf
itcmdr offsite admin server
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-adminsvr [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
\&
Commands:
  serve          Run the admin API and the SiteLink
  init           Console, once: create the first owner and print their enrollment code
  recover\-owner  Console: fresh owner enrollment code when every owner device and the words are lost
  audit\-verify   Check the audit hash chain
  tls\-status     v1.1.0: the admin API certificate (mode, expiry, last renewal, last error)
  backup         v1.2.0: adminsvr's own backups (its database, keys, TLS, ACME and settings; never site backups)
  restore        v1.2.0: restore adminsvr from one of its own backups (recovery words on stdin; stop the service first)
  help           Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
\&
Options:
      \-\-env\-file <ENV_FILE>
          KEY=VALUE settings file (read before the other flags; the environment wins) [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ENV_FILE=] [default: ""]
      \-\-db\-url <DB_URL>
          Database: postgres://user:pass@host/db, or sqlite://<path> (default: SQLite in the data dir) [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_DB_URL=] [default: ""]
      \-\-data\-dir <DATA_DIR>
          [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_DATA_DIR=] [default: /var/lib/itcmdr\-adminsvr]
      \-\-api\-addr <API_ADDR>
          [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_API_ADDR=] [default: 0.0.0.0:8444]
      \-\-site\-addr <SITE_ADDR>
          [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_SITE_ADDR=] [default: 0.0.0.0:8443]
      \-\-public\-api <PUBLIC_API>
          host:port clients use to reach the API (put into enrollment codes) [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_PUBLIC_API=] [default: ""]
      \-\-public\-site <PUBLIC_SITE>
          host:port sites use to reach the SiteLink (put into site tokens) [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_PUBLIC_SITE=] [default: ""]
      \-\-tls\-names <TLS_NAMES>
          extra TLS certificate names, comma separated [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_TLS_NAMES=] [default: ""]
      \-\-heartbeat\-secs <HEARTBEAT_SECS>
          [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_HEARTBEAT_SECS=] [default: 60]
      \-\-site\-missed <SITE_MISSED>
          [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_SITE_MISSED=] [default: 5]
      \-\-rp\-id <RP_ID>
          WebAuthn RP id for passkeys (default: the host of \-\-public\-api) [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_RP_ID=] [default: ""]
      \-\-web\-origins <WEB_ORIGINS>
          Extra WebAuthn origins (the web app), comma separated [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_WEB_ORIGINS=] [default: ""]
      \-\-fcm\-service\-account <FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT>
          Push (FCM): Firebase service account JSON file [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=] [default: ""]
      \-\-fcm\-url <FCM_URL>
          [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_FCM_URL=] [default: ""]
      \-\-apns\-key <APNS_KEY>
          Push (APNs): the .p8 auth key file [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_APNS_KEY=] [default: ""]
      \-\-apns\-key\-id <APNS_KEY_ID>
          [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_APNS_KEY_ID=] [default: ""]
      \-\-apns\-team\-id <APNS_TEAM_ID>
          [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_APNS_TEAM_ID=] [default: ""]
      \-\-apns\-topic <APNS_TOPIC>
          The admin app's bundle id [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_APNS_TOPIC=] [default: ""]
      \-\-apns\-url <APNS_URL>
          [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_APNS_URL=] [default: ""]
      \-\-push\-min\-severity <PUSH_MIN_SEVERITY>
          Lowest alert severity that is pushed: critical | cautious | informational [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_PUSH_MIN_SEVERITY=] [default: cautious]
      \-\-acme\-domains <ACME_DOMAINS>
          v1.1.0 ACME (Let's Encrypt) for the admin API: certificate names, comma separated (empty = off) [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ACME_DOMAINS=] [default: ""]
      \-\-acme\-contact <ACME_CONTACT>
          Contact e\-mail(s) for the ACME account, comma separated [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ACME_CONTACT=] [default: ""]
      \-\-acme\-directory <ACME_DIRECTORY>
          production | staging | an ACME directory URL [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ACME_DIRECTORY=] [default: production]
      \-\-acme\-directory\-root <ACME_DIRECTORY_ROOT>
          PEM root for the ACME directory's own HTTPS (only for test CAs such as Pebble) [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ACME_DIRECTORY_ROOT=] [default: ""]
      \-\-acme\-challenge <ACME_CHALLENGE>
          tls\-alpn\-01 (on the admin API port; forward 443 to it) | http\-01 (on \-\-acme\-http\-addr) [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ACME_CHALLENGE=] [default: tls\-alpn\-01]
      \-\-acme\-http\-addr <ACME_HTTP_ADDR>
          [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ACME_HTTP_ADDR=] [default: 0.0.0.0:80]
      \-\-acme\-cache\-dir <ACME_CACHE_DIR>
          Account key and certificate (default <data dir>/acme, 0700) [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ACME_CACHE_DIR=] [default: ""]
      \-\-acme\-renew\-days <ACME_RENEW_DAYS>
          [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ACME_RENEW_DAYS=] [default: 30]
      \-\-acme\-retry\-secs <ACME_RETRY_SECS>
          [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ACME_RETRY_SECS=] [default: 3600]
      \-\-backup\-dir <BACKUP_DIR>
          v1.2.0 adminsvr's own backups: archive folder (default <data dir>/backups) [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_BACKUP_DIR=] [default: ""]
      \-\-backup\-hour <BACKUP_HOUR>
          Nightly backup hour (0\-23, local time) while serving, or `off` [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_BACKUP_HOUR=] [default: 3]
      \-\-backup\-keep <BACKUP_KEEP>
          Nightly archives kept (manual archives are never pruned) [env: ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_BACKUP_KEEP=] [default: 14]
  \-h, \-\-help
          Print help
  \-V, \-\-version
          Print version
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-adminsvr serve
.nf
Run the admin API and the SiteLink
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-adminsvr serve
\&
Options:
  \-h, \-\-help  Print help
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-adminsvr init
.nf
Console, once: create the first owner and print their enrollment code
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-adminsvr init \-\-email <EMAIL> \-\-name <NAME>
\&
Options:
      \-\-email <EMAIL>  
      \-\-name <NAME>    
  \-h, \-\-help           Print help
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-adminsvr recover\-owner
.nf
Console: fresh owner enrollment code when every owner device and the words are lost
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-adminsvr recover\-owner \-\-email <EMAIL>
\&
Options:
      \-\-email <EMAIL>  
  \-h, \-\-help           Print help
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-adminsvr audit\-verify
.nf
Check the audit hash chain
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-adminsvr audit\-verify
\&
Options:
  \-h, \-\-help  Print help
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-adminsvr tls\-status
.nf
v1.1.0: the admin API certificate (mode, expiry, last renewal, last error)
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-adminsvr tls\-status
\&
Options:
  \-h, \-\-help  Print help
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-adminsvr backup
.nf
v1.2.0: adminsvr's own backups (its database, keys, TLS, ACME and settings; never site backups)
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-adminsvr backup <COMMAND>
\&
Commands:
  init    Set up backups: print 24 new recovery words ONCE (write them down; they are never stored)
  create  Make a backup now
  list    List the backups
  verify  Check a backup: signature and hash; \-\-deep (words on stdin) also decrypts and checks every file
  drill   Restore drill: check the newest backup without touching the live install; \-\-deep (words on stdin) also decrypts it and restores it into a throwaway database
  prune   Delete old nightly backups (keeps \-\-backup\-keep)
  status  Recovery key, last backup and last drill
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
\&
Options:
  \-h, \-\-help  Print help
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-adminsvr backup init
.nf
Set up backups: print 24 new recovery words ONCE (write them down; they are never stored)
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-adminsvr backup init [OPTIONS]
\&
Options:
      \-\-replace  Issue new words (archives made before still need the old words)
  \-h, \-\-help     Print help
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-adminsvr backup create
.nf
Make a backup now
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-adminsvr backup create [OPTIONS]
\&
Options:
      \-\-out <OUT>  Write it here instead of the backup folder
  \-h, \-\-help       Print help
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-adminsvr backup list
.nf
List the backups
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-adminsvr backup list [OPTIONS]
\&
Options:
      \-\-dir <DIR>  
  \-h, \-\-help       Print help
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-adminsvr backup verify
.nf
Check a backup: signature and hash; \-\-deep (words on stdin) also decrypts and checks every file
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-adminsvr backup verify [OPTIONS] <ARCHIVE>
\&
Arguments:
  <ARCHIVE>  
\&
Options:
      \-\-deep  
  \-h, \-\-help  Print help
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-adminsvr backup drill
.nf
Restore drill: check the newest backup without touching the live install; \-\-deep (words on stdin) also decrypts it and restores it into a throwaway database
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-adminsvr backup drill [OPTIONS]
\&
Options:
      \-\-deep       
      \-\-dir <DIR>  
  \-h, \-\-help       Print help
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-adminsvr backup prune
.nf
Delete old nightly backups (keeps \-\-backup\-keep)
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-adminsvr backup prune [OPTIONS]
\&
Options:
      \-\-dir <DIR>  
  \-h, \-\-help       Print help
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-adminsvr backup status
.nf
Recovery key, last backup and last drill
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-adminsvr backup status
\&
Options:
  \-h, \-\-help  Print help
.fi
.SH COMMAND: itcmdr\-adminsvr restore
.nf
v1.2.0: restore adminsvr from one of its own backups (recovery words on stdin; stop the service first)
\&
Usage: itcmdr\-adminsvr restore [OPTIONS] \-\-from <FROM>
\&
Options:
      \-\-from <FROM>  The archive (.itcab)
      \-\-dry\-run      Open and check everything, show what would be written, change nothing
  \-h, \-\-help         Print help
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ENV_FILE
KEY=VALUE settings file
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_DB_URL
postgres://... or sqlite://<path> (default SQLite in the data folder)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_DATA_DIR
data folder (default /var/lib/itcmdr\-adminsvr)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_API_ADDR
admin API listen address (default 0.0.0.0:8444)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_SITE_ADDR
SiteLink listen address (default 0.0.0.0:8443)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_PUBLIC_API
host:port clients use (put into enrollment codes)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_PUBLIC_SITE
host:port sites use (put into site tokens)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_TLS_NAMES
extra internal certificate names, comma separated
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_HEARTBEAT_SECS
site status interval (default 60)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_SITE_MISSED
missed heartbeats before a site is down (default 5)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_RP_ID
WebAuthn RP id (default: the host of the public API)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_WEB_ORIGINS
extra WebAuthn origins, comma separated
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT
Firebase service account JSON (push to Android)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_FCM_URL
FCM endpoint override
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_APNS_KEY
APNs .p8 auth key file
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_APNS_KEY_ID
APNs key id
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_APNS_TEAM_ID
Apple team id
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_APNS_TOPIC
the admin app's bundle id
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_APNS_URL
APNs endpoint (sandbox for development builds)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_PUSH_MIN_SEVERITY
lowest pushed severity (default cautious)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ACME_DOMAINS
Let's Encrypt names for the admin API, comma separated (empty = off)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ACME_CONTACT
ACME account contact e\-mail(s)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ACME_DIRECTORY
production, staging or a directory URL (default production)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ACME_DIRECTORY_ROOT
PEM root for a test CA's directory
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ACME_CHALLENGE
tls\-alpn\-01 (default) or http\-01
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ACME_HTTP_ADDR
HTTP\-01 listener (default 0.0.0.0:80)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ACME_CACHE_DIR
account key and certificate (default <data dir>/acme)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ACME_RENEW_DAYS
renew this many days before expiry (default 30)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_ACME_RETRY_SECS
wait after a failed attempt (default 3600)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_BACKUP_DIR
v1.2.0 folder for adminsvr's own backups (default <data dir>/backups; [adminsvr backup](BACKUP\-ADMINSVR.md))
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_BACKUP_HOUR
nightly backup hour, 0\-23 local, or off (default 3)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_ADMINSVR_BACKUP_KEEP
nightly backups kept (default 14; manual ones are never pruned)
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBitcmdr\fR(7), docs/README.md (also the in-app help: \fBitcmdr-cli help\fR, \fBitcmdr-admin help\fR)
